          "sourceContextAndLimits": "Original SH2022 physical/printed50 conditions particle-colour reasoning on choosing dyes;68-70 preserve GK optional extra dye theme and LK conditional dye duty with an alternative further Chemie-und-Leben theme. Page70 left column has colour mixing, dye classes, fibre/dye/process relation and one example dyeing process; right column adds electrophilic substitution and substituent effects at increased level. No unique vat method, industrial-history case or acid-base-plus-redox indicator pair is prescribed as a universal whole P.",
          "wholeUnchangedAcquisitionScope": "Whole economic P: supplied synthetic output/price/research/archive models; scale-up/knowledge transfer, causal confounders, percentage versus total revenue and missing environmental costs. No real firm archive or universal single-cause history is asserted. The separate requires proposal retains all this performance.",
          "compilerScopeSemantics": "Only this supported jurisdiction is an explicit own-acquisition scope input. Current tags and unchanged listed authored views limit course placement; metadata is not stage/course enforcement, and views remain CrossStage. Raw applicability is the before-field, not a new compiled pass.",
          "ownerPolicyBoundary": "Include already authored Chemistry topics before the later topic-choice flow; preserve official optionality and do not claim a learner selected a theme.",
          "nativeAndPerformanceBoundary": "Full source/route/P/D/M/native bindings and actual learner/teacher execution remain separate. No actual experiment or research completion is claimed."
        },
